    "created_at": "2015-10-06T04:01:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-06T04:01:23Z",
    "body": "I'd be ok with a UA style sheet exception (either way, I guess).  Making the UA stylesheet entirely case-sensitive unless <code>i</code> is used seems a bit error-prone, both in specs and implementations.\n\nGecko currently implements the handling of the type attribute in C++ code (see HTMLLIElement::ParseAttribute and HTMLSharedListElement::ParseAttribute).\n\nNote that we support case-sensitive type attributes on <code>ul</code> as well.  We also appear to support {upper,lower}-{roman,alpha} on ol and ul, but not li.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
