    "created_at": "2015-10-06T16:17:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-06T16:17:20Z",
    "body": "On Tuesday 2015-10-06 01:07 -0700, Simon Pieters wrote:\n\n> I noticed one more thing. The case-insensitive thing does not apply to XHTML per spec, but certainly we want the UA stylesheet to work right for uppercase values in XHTML. So we need to continue to use `i` in the UA stylesheet.\n\nWork right for which uppercase values?  My understanding was that\nmany attribute values were really intended to be lowercase-only in\nXHTML.  (Though obviously type=\"A\" and type=\"I\" would be\nuppercase-only.)\n\n## \n\n𝄞   L. David Baron                         http://dbaron.org/   𝄂\n𝄢   Mozilla                          https://www.mozilla.org/   𝄂\n             Before I built a wall I'd ask to know\n             What I was walling in or walling out,\n             And to whom I was like to give offense.\n               - Robert Frost, Mending Wall (1914)\n",
